            <ArticleTitle>Malignant cylindroma of the external auditory canal.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>97-101</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This report describes a case of a malignant cylindroma arising in the external auditory canal.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="STUDY DESIGN" NlmCategory="METHODS">Retrospective surgical case review.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SETTING" NlmCategory="METHODS">Tertiary care teaching hospital.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="INTERVENTION" NlmCategory="METHODS">Wide local excision with margin control.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Local control of disease at 2-year follow-up.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">To our knowledge, this is the first report describing a malignant degeneration of cylindroma in the external auditory canal. This tumor represents an extremely rare cutaneous neoplasm, thus raising diagnostic and therapeutic challenges.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
